            "theoryHtml": "\n<p><strong>Geographical Position of India:</strong>\nIndia is situated entirely in the <strong>Northern Hemisphere</strong> latitudinally and in the <strong>Eastern Hemisphere</strong> longitudinally. Geomorphologically, it occupies the south-central peninsula of the Asian continent, extending southward into the Indian Ocean between the Arabian Sea on the west and the Bay of Bengal on the east.</p>\n<p><strong>Spatial Dimensions & Latitudinal-Longitudinal Coordinates:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Latitudinal Extent:</strong>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Mainland India extends from <strong>$8^\\circ 4'\\text{ N}$</strong> (Cape Comorin, Kanyakumari, Tamil Nadu) in the south to <strong>$37^\\circ 6'\\text{ N}$</strong> (Indira Col, Ladakh) in the north.</li>\n    <li>Total latitudinal span is approximately <strong>$29^\\circ 2'$</strong> (nearly $30^\\circ$).</li>\n    <li>If the Andaman and Nicobar Islands are included, the southernmost territory of the Indian Union extends down to <strong>$6^\\circ 45'\\text{ N}$</strong> (Indira Point on Great Nicobar Island).</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Longitudinal Extent:</strong>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Extends from <strong>$68^\\circ 7'\\text{ E}$</strong> (Guhar Moti / Sir Creek, Kutch, Gujarat) in the west to <strong>$97^\\circ 25'\\text{ E}$</strong> (Kibithu, Anjaw district, Arunachal Pradesh) in the east.</li>\n    <li>Total longitudinal span is approximately <strong>$29^\\circ 18'$</strong> (nearly $30^\\circ$).</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>North-South & East-West Distance Distinctions:</strong>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>North to South Distance:</strong> From Indira Col in Ladakh to Kanyakumari in Tamil Nadu is exactly <strong>$3,214\\text{ km}$</strong>.</li>\n    <li><strong>East to West Distance:</strong> From Kibithu in Arunachal Pradesh to Guhar Moti in Gujarat is exactly <strong>$2,933\\text{ km}$</strong>.</li>\n    <li><em>Geographical Reason for Distance Disparity:</em> Although both latitudinal and longitudinal spans are nearly identical ($\\approx 30^\\circ$), the north-south distance ($3,214\\text{ km}$) exceeds the east-west distance ($2,933\\text{ km}$) because lines of latitude are parallel and maintain a constant distance (~$111\\text{ km}$ per degree), whereas lines of longitude converge toward the poles, causing the distance between consecutive meridians to decrease progressively from the Equator (~$111.3\\text{ km}$) to the poles ($0\\text{ km}$).</li>\n  </ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n<p><strong>Surface Area & Global Standing:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Total Land Area:</strong> India encompasses an area of <strong>$3,287,263\\text{ sq km}$</strong> ($3.287\\text{ million sq km}$).</li>\n<li><strong>Global Land Share:</strong> Represents approximately <strong>$2.42\\%$</strong> (commonly cited as $2.4\\%$) of the total geographical land area of the world.</li>\n<li><strong>World Rank by Area (7th Position):</strong>\n  <ol>\n    <li>Russia ($17.09\\text{ million sq km}$)</li>\n    <li>Canada ($9.98\\text{ million sq km}$)</li>\n    <li>United States of America ($9.83\\text{ million sq km}$)</li>\n    <li>China ($9.60\\text{ million sq km}$)</li>\n    <li>Brazil ($8.51\\text{ million sq km}$)</li>\n    <li>Australia ($7.69\\text{ million sq km}$)</li>\n    <li><strong>India ($3.287\\text{ million sq km}$)</strong></li>\n  </ol>\n  <em>Subsequent nations:</em> 8th Argentina, 9th Kazakhstan (largest landlocked country), 10th Algeria (largest in Africa).\n</li>\n<li><strong>Global Population Share:</strong> Houses over $17.5\\%$ of the world's population, ranking <strong>1st in the world</strong> (surpassing China as per UN DESA 2023 estimates).</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n<p><strong>The Two-Hour Time Lag:</strong>\nBecause the Earth rotates $360^\\circ$ on its axis in 24 hours:\n$$1^\\circ\\text{ of longitude} = \\frac{24 \\times 60\\text{ minutes}}{360} = \\mathbf{4\\text{ minutes}}$$\nWith a longitudinal span of nearly $30^\\circ$ ($97^\\circ 25' - 68^\\circ 7' \\approx 29^\\circ 18'$):\n$$\\text{Time difference} \\approx 30 \\times 4\\text{ minutes} = 120\\text{ minutes} = \\mathbf{2\\text{ hours}}$$\nConsequently, the Sun rises approximately <strong>two hours earlier</strong> in Dong/Kibithu (Arunachal Pradesh) than in Dwarka/Guhar Moti (Gujarat).</p>\n",
